{#
  Custom incident-response prompt template for AIHandler.

  Point AIHandler at this file with:
    LOGSCRIBE_JINJA_TEMPLATE_DIR=examples/templates
    LOGSCRIBE_JINJA_LOG_PROMPT_TEMPLATE_NAME=incident_prompt.jinja2

  Variables available (same as logscribe/templates/default_log_prompt.jinja2):
  - logs: a list of log record dictionaries, each with keys like
    timestamp, levelname, message, pathname, funcName, lineno,
    exception_info (if any), stack_info (if any), extras (if any).
#}
You are an on-call engineer triaging the following batch of application log records.
Respond using exactly these three labeled sections:

SEVERITY: <one word -- LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, or CRITICAL>
ROOT CAUSE: <your best hypothesis, in one or two sentences>
SUGGESTED ACTION: <a concrete next step for the on-call engineer>

Log Batch ({{ logs|length }} records):
==================================================

{% for log_entry in logs %}
Timestamp: {{ log_entry.timestamp }}
Level:     {{ log_entry.levelname }}
Message:   {{ log_entry.message }}
{% if log_entry.exception_info %}
Exception Info:
{{ log_entry.exception_info|indent(2, true) }}
{% endif %}
--------------------------------------------------
{% endfor %}
